.SH "CHARACTER CLASSES"
.sp
.RS 4
.PD 0
.TP 11
\f(CI[...]\fP
.ad l
Positive character class
.TP 11
\f(CI[^...]\fP
.ad l
Negative character class
.TP 11
\f(CI[x\-y]\fP
.ad l
Range (can be used for hexadecimal characters)
.TP 11
\f(CI[[:\fP\f(CIxxx\fP\f(CI:]]\fP
.ad l
Positive POSIX named set
.TP 11
\f(CI[[:^\fP\f(CIxxx\fP\f(CI:]]\fP
.ad l
Negative POSIX named set
.PD
.RE
.PP
.ad l
.sp
The recognized POSIX named sets are:
.sp
.RS 4
.PD 0
.TP 7
\f(CIalnum\fP
.ad l
Alphanumeric
.TP 7
\f(CIalpha\fP
.ad l
Alphabetic
.TP 7
\f(CIascii\fP
.ad l
0\(en127
.TP 7
\f(CIblank\fP
.ad l
Space or tab
.TP 7
\f(CIcntrl\fP
.ad l
Control character
.TP 7
\f(CIdigit\fP
.ad l
Decimal digit
.TP 7
\f(CIgraph\fP
.ad l
