.SH "BACKTRACKING CONTROL"
.sp
All backtracking control verbs may be in the form \f(CI(*VERB:\fP\f(CINAME\fP\f(CI)\fP. For \f(CI(*MARK)\fP the
name is mandatory, for the others it is optional. \f(CI(*SKIP)\fP changes its behaviour
if \f(CI:\fP\f(CINAME\fP is present. The others just set a name for passing back to the caller,
but this is not a name that \f(CI(*SKIP)\fP can see. The following act immediately they
are reached:
.sp
